        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "22d2c115-83f1-3759-ab50-50fd42877cb1",
                "word": "languide",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "db44dd38-a07c-4ad6-8046-bce10805e0d4",
                        "entry_id": "22d2c115-83f1-3759-ab50-50fd42877cb1",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "masculine",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "languides"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "463b5ce2-323d-305c-ac83-53c8fa2c6957",
                        "entry_id": "22d2c115-83f1-3759-ab50-50fd42877cb1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "En parlant d’une personne :"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ca63372a-fb60-3520-95d1-7753be93563c",
                        "entry_id": "22d2c115-83f1-3759-ab50-50fd42877cb1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "En parlant d’une personne :",
                            "Qui est dans un état habituel de langueur, qui dépérit, qui se trouve dans un état d’abattement, de grande faiblesse physique et psychologique."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "literary"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "23d70be7-60d7-4dbb-8a45-c663c7c05be9",
                                "sense_id": "ca63372a-fb60-3520-95d1-7753be93563c",
                                "text": "Ô gazons animés par un vivant zéphyr !\nPlantes, arbres géants, atmosphères languides,\nCieux d’opale et toi, mer, de ton mystère avide,\nQue mon âme, de vous, pourra-t-elle s’emplir."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d47c06a4-2448-37a9-88b4-8ccf12073cf0",
                        "entry_id": "22d2c115-83f1-3759-ab50-50fd42877cb1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "En parlant d’une personne :",
                            "Qui exprime un sentiment de langueur."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "055a6897-d8d6-41d3-911a-b8b79b9a4ff7",
                                "sense_id": "d47c06a4-2448-37a9-88b4-8ccf12073cf0",
                                "text": "Il passa cette dernière journée en compagnie des siens, tout imprégné de la tristesse languide qui suit les renoncements."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "eb159a13-a2a6-4407-9fb2-336100d76729",
                                "sense_id": "d47c06a4-2448-37a9-88b4-8ccf12073cf0",
                                "text": "… ; vous l’avez enfin la femme de l’Empire du Lever du Soleil, en sa grâce languide, et en son coquet rampement sur les nattes du parquet."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c2fd0d37-4d35-3344-8999-f37cc7e58335",
                        "entry_id": "22d2c115-83f1-3759-ab50-50fd42877cb1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "En parlant d’une chose :"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "df4accbf-5a6c-310f-a654-aa5d288e95c1",
                        "entry_id": "22d2c115-83f1-3759-ab50-50fd42877cb1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "En parlant d’une chose :",
                            "Qui manque de force, d’énergie."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5cc97ff2-a46e-492a-a87b-e99b3c3a8309",
                                "sense_id": "df4accbf-5a6c-310f-a654-aa5d288e95c1",
                                "text": "Le calme des plaines grises, toujours moites de brume au matin, ressemblait à ces aubes d’été languides qui se traînent comme assommées sous une fin d’orage."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4cba0b64-48ea-490e-8bca-4672f18dfa6f",
                                "sense_id": "df4accbf-5a6c-310f-a654-aa5d288e95c1",
                                "text": "Je lisais L’Adieu à l’adolescence de Mauriac, j’en apprenais par cœur de longs passages languides que je me récitais dans les rues."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e09db66a-2bae-44ea-ad9a-82a28d969b6a",
                                "sense_id": "df4accbf-5a6c-310f-a654-aa5d288e95c1",
                                "text": "Et puis, nous sommes moins belliqueux qu’aux siècles héroïques. Nous luttons mollement, avec une languide indifférence et parfois nous ne faisons même pas trop grise mine à l’ennemi qui est déjà dans nos murs."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5677946e-5ad5-4a9b-aeae-ca374c8060ea",
                                "sense_id": "df4accbf-5a6c-310f-a654-aa5d288e95c1",
                                "text": "L’odeur fraîche de l’ail, acide de la roquette, l’odeur plus entêtante et languide du melon, l’odeur fauve du marché à la volaille."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b7c2c7d4-6962-4b99-8823-c9c1f08c9bd6",
                                "sense_id": "df4accbf-5a6c-310f-a654-aa5d288e95c1",
                                "text": "Il avait demandé par testament d'être ramené au Sarawak,quel que soit le lieu où il mourrait, pour être enterré au milieu du peuple qu'il aimait, non loin du fleuve au cours languide\""
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d5d2aa3e-c68d-3e0c-9fb8-0d891c1d7f87",
                        "entry_id": "22d2c115-83f1-3759-ab50-50fd42877cb1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "En parlant d’une chose :",
                            "Qui évoque, engendre la langueur."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9d3202ea-bb8b-4c95-8fe9-eae1e9aaa238",
                        "source_entry_id": "22d2c115-83f1-3759-ab50-50fd42877cb1",
                        "target_lang_word": "lackadaisical",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "lackadaisical",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ee398392-b386-3fdf-a36c-24d96fb1b649",
                                        "entry_id": "5cfa6bea-fa29-3285-b628-1a4614e34c57",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Showing no interest, vigor, determination, or enthusiasm."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c99ab475-8dd0-4843-a491-ef9ec3a28d0a",
                                                "sense_id": "ee398392-b386-3fdf-a36c-24d96fb1b649",
                                                "text": "the lackadaisical look on his face"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1174f5eb-7f0b-4f7e-96cc-4991b77e6660",
                                                "sense_id": "ee398392-b386-3fdf-a36c-24d96fb1b649",
                                                "text": "I, at one time, used to go and take a hand at cribbage with a friend, and afterwards discuss a cold sirloin of beef, and throw out a few lackadaisical remarks, in a way to please myself, but it would not do long."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5b8265dc-9d9b-47d9-ace4-da5db72702ca",
                                                "sense_id": "ee398392-b386-3fdf-a36c-24d96fb1b649",
                                                "text": "\"Then let those who do know it learn that you are able to bear such wounds without outward complaint. I tell you fairly that I cannot sympathize with a lackadaisical lover.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "94033d5e-6180-4f8e-8250-5c6705fb8a6b",
                                                "sense_id": "ee398392-b386-3fdf-a36c-24d96fb1b649",
                                                "text": "I could hear the sound of the janitor's lackadaisical scrubbing against the wooden floor."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "af96274f-a1ea-36db-a4dc-466711e803b5",
                                        "entry_id": "5cfa6bea-fa29-3285-b628-1a4614e34c57",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Lazy; slothful; indolent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ba22831b-6be5-4fb4-8dd6-e30a04db562a",
                        "source_entry_id": "22d2c115-83f1-3759-ab50-50fd42877cb1",
                        "target_lang_word": "languid",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "languid",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4bb1db1f-12b6-308c-abfc-79c3855a62d2",
                                        "entry_id": "7d153ca7-cd66-350a-8974-6460e97bfeb1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of a person or animal, or their body functions: flagging from weakness, or inactive or weak, especially due to illness or tiredness; faint, listless."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d73f8619-e24b-4fa8-96b0-8aa9e70c1a5b",
                                                "sense_id": "4bb1db1f-12b6-308c-abfc-79c3855a62d2",
                                                "text": "[T]he ſalt of vipers is alſo thought to exceed any other animal ſalt vvhatever, in giving vigour to the languid circulation, and prompting to venery."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1787692d-9696-4f2b-98c0-5d9075fbe42b",
                                                "sense_id": "4bb1db1f-12b6-308c-abfc-79c3855a62d2",
                                                "text": "At first she \"ran a temperature\" in American parlance, and I could not resist the exquisite caloricity of unexpected delights—Venus febriculosa—though it was a very languid Lolita that moaned and coughed and shivered in my embrace."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "78060a47-fffa-398a-a2d2-e4f68b72b910",
                                        "entry_id": "7d153ca7-cd66-350a-8974-6460e97bfeb1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of a person or their movement: showing a dislike for physical effort; leisurely, unhurried."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7e44d731-63f3-46f9-9314-2b01888d8cc0",
                                                "sense_id": "78060a47-fffa-398a-a2d2-e4f68b72b910",
                                                "text": "Loth was he to move / From the imprinted couch, and when he did, / 'Twas with slow, languid paces, and face hid / In muffling hands."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c6d4efab-712f-441a-be1c-9472f990329d",
                                                "sense_id": "78060a47-fffa-398a-a2d2-e4f68b72b910",
                                                "text": "A consort was found for him in the royal family of France; and her beauty and grace gave him a languid pleasure."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "840aeccc-72df-4778-bc0f-6d99a1dcd80e",
                                                "sense_id": "78060a47-fffa-398a-a2d2-e4f68b72b910",
                                                "text": "Val watched his back, languid and slim, till it was out of sight …"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "53cb5e7f-fe74-44ef-a500-b71b1c938d2d",
                                                "sense_id": "78060a47-fffa-398a-a2d2-e4f68b72b910",
                                                "text": "Darkness fell before we reached the Belgian frontier, and on through the night our train took her languid way."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cf34592b-f0e2-3995-a712-57c93d29bdad",
                                        "entry_id": "7d153ca7-cd66-350a-8974-6460e97bfeb1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of a person or their actions, character, etc.: lacking drive, emotion, or enthusiasm; apathetic, listless, spiritless, unenthusiastic."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "744ef3c8-015a-49a4-a1d3-65e0a125851e",
                                                "sense_id": "cf34592b-f0e2-3995-a712-57c93d29bdad",
                                                "text": "VVith ſecret Checks her languid Soule ſhe chid / VVhich vvith ſuch violence never yet did flame; / Her Eyes hung dovvn; her Cheeks vvere over-ſpread / VVith bluſhing (but vvith ô hovv guiltleſſe!) ſhame: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "27232648-a1f7-4625-adc4-ff2a28747397",
                                                "sense_id": "cf34592b-f0e2-3995-a712-57c93d29bdad",
                                                "text": "I'll haſten to my Troops, / And fire their languid Souls with Cato’s Virtue; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c59dd95f-7f7e-4cf0-a0f6-26fbbb4850e5",
                                                "sense_id": "cf34592b-f0e2-3995-a712-57c93d29bdad",
                                                "text": "[A] Harlot form ſoft-ſliding by, / VVith mincing ſtep, ſmall voice, and languid eye; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "33366c22-b20a-42b7-828c-a53985c04065",
                                                "sense_id": "cf34592b-f0e2-3995-a712-57c93d29bdad",
                                                "text": "Far from any thing inflam[ma]tory, I never heard a more languid debate in this Houſe."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a355f7b7-7913-451c-a63a-aab4337c19ac",
                                                "sense_id": "cf34592b-f0e2-3995-a712-57c93d29bdad",
                                                "text": "I was languid and dull and very bad company when I wrote the above; I am better now, to my own feelings at least, and wish I may be more agreeable."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5b0faaed-3c4f-4fc3-b2bc-096beb69e1c2",
                                                "sense_id": "cf34592b-f0e2-3995-a712-57c93d29bdad",
                                                "text": "George had an air at once swaggering and melancholy, languid and fierce."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fbd1f01d-f37b-4d2b-a792-a919c6d62077",
                                                "sense_id": "cf34592b-f0e2-3995-a712-57c93d29bdad",
                                                "text": "Too lazy or too languid where only his own interests were at stake—touch his benevolence, and all the wheels of the clockwork felt the impetus of the master-spring."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9fb472ee-1bec-36da-8852-c741bbf00de8",
                                        "entry_id": "7d153ca7-cd66-350a-8974-6460e97bfeb1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of a colour: not bright; dull, muted."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4f980e33-dc61-35fd-8d67-79599c8dbf5a",
                                        "entry_id": "7d153ca7-cd66-350a-8974-6460e97bfeb1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of an idea, writing, etc.: dull, uninteresting."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dc37b718-06dd-4b26-9129-64f7eb5695b4",
                                                "sense_id": "4f980e33-dc61-35fd-8d67-79599c8dbf5a",
                                                "text": "[S]ome very languid remarks on the probable brilliancy of the ball were all that broke, at intervals, a silence of half-an-hour, before they were joined by the master of the house."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "928dc505-a79c-4244-a599-0d7645f25377",
                                                "sense_id": "4f980e33-dc61-35fd-8d67-79599c8dbf5a",
                                                "text": "He had written certain thin Books, all of a thin languid nature; but rational, clear; especially a Book of Fables in Verse, which are watery, but not wholly water, and have still a languid flavour in them for readers."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a2722093-ad16-36c0-a0cb-d7e58fa186f1",
                                        "entry_id": "7d153ca7-cd66-350a-8974-6460e97bfeb1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of a period of time: characterized by lack of activity; pleasant and relaxed; unstressful."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e5b2b813-82b7-4a74-87b6-c682a41d5336",
                                                "sense_id": "a2722093-ad16-36c0-a0cb-d7e58fa186f1",
                                                "text": "Unknown to them, when ſenſual pleaſures cloy, / To fill the languid pauſe with finer joy; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "01ceb7ef-b8cf-4051-b99c-9dbb99006948",
                                                "sense_id": "a2722093-ad16-36c0-a0cb-d7e58fa186f1",
                                                "text": "Toil is the portion of day, as sleep is that of night; but if there be one hour of the twenty-four which has the life of day without its labour, and the rest of night without its slumber, it is the lovely and languid hour of twilight."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fba1b630-ad1a-337e-8100-8b8d3a6e3605",
                                        "entry_id": "7d153ca7-cd66-350a-8974-6460e97bfeb1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of a thing: lacking energy, liveliness, or strength; inactive, slow-moving, weak."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1bf458b4-8cd6-47ec-b846-2894ea5fdfab",
                                                "sense_id": "fba1b630-ad1a-337e-8100-8b8d3a6e3605",
                                                "text": "languid breathing    languid movements"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "37a04f9a-1ebd-48f7-bbd8-4cb5835b93ee",
                                                "sense_id": "fba1b630-ad1a-337e-8100-8b8d3a6e3605",
                                                "text": "[T]he ſound [of bees or flies] is ſtrongeſt in dry vveather, and very vveake in rainy ſeaſon, and tovvard vvinter; for then the ayre is moyſt, and the invvard ſpirit grovving vveake, makes a languid and dumbe alliſion upon the parts."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f42b06e8-68b5-4a81-aa59-ea1e6a2842ca",
                                                "sense_id": "fba1b630-ad1a-337e-8100-8b8d3a6e3605",
                                                "text": "[W]hen the languid Flames at length ſubſide, / He ſtrovvs a Bed of glovving Embers vvide, / Above the Coals the ſmoaking Fragments turns, / And ſprinkles ſacred Salt from lifted Urns; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fb93b8a5-064e-4c60-8ae7-80cd56f9e863",
                                                "sense_id": "fba1b630-ad1a-337e-8100-8b8d3a6e3605",
                                                "text": "As love vvithout eſteem, is volatile and capricious; eſteem vvithout love, is languid and cold."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a764d36c-bd5e-4b49-9362-68cf596e29c0",
                                                "sense_id": "fba1b630-ad1a-337e-8100-8b8d3a6e3605",
                                                "text": "I knew the flowers, I knew the leaves, I knew / The tearful glimmer of the languid dawn / On those long, rank, dark woodwalks drenched in dew, / Leading from lawn to lawn."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "36a3c9d1-cea6-4302-95a6-5486e22da921",
                                                "sense_id": "fba1b630-ad1a-337e-8100-8b8d3a6e3605",
                                                "text": "His thick, heavy, languid, lustreless black hair fell down behind his ears on to his shoulders, in that musicianlike way that is so offensive to the normal Englishman."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
